<article class="env-lemma" id="0E2E">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E2E">Lemma <span data-tag="0E2E">47.27.3</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : R \to A$ be a flat finite type ring map of Noetherian rings. Then the relative dualizing complex $\omega _{A/R}^\bullet = \varphi ^!(R)$ of Section <a href="/tag/0E9M" data-tag="0E9M">47.25</a> is a relative dualizing complex in the sense of Definition <a href="/tag/0E2C" data-tag="0E2C">47.27.1</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      From Lemma <a href="/tag/0BZW" data-tag="0BZW">47.25.2</a> we see that $\varphi ^!(R)$ is $R$-perfect. Denote $\delta : A \otimes _ R A \to A$ the multiplication map and $p_1, p_2 : A \to A \otimes _ R A$ the coprojections. Then 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \varphi ^!(R) \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} (A \otimes _ R A) = \varphi ^!(R) \otimes _{A, p_1}^\mathbf {L} (A \otimes _ R A) = p_2^!(A)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by Lemma <a href="/tag/0BZN" data-tag="0BZN">47.24.4</a>. Recall that $ R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{A \otimes _ R A}(A, \varphi ^!(R) \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} (A \otimes _ R A)) $ is the image of $\delta ^!(\varphi ^!(R) \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} (A \otimes _ R A))$ under the restriction map $\delta _* : D(A) \to D(A \otimes _ R A)$. Use the definition of $\delta ^!$ from Section <a href="/tag/0BZI" data-tag="0BZI">47.24</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/0A71" data-tag="0A71">47.13.3</a>. Since $\delta ^!(p_2^!(A)) \cong A$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0BZT" data-tag="0BZT">47.24.7</a> we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>